{"tool_name":"structalign","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"StructAlign","home":"http://mouse.genebee.msu.ru/tools/StructAlign.html","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Program for alignment of structures of DNA-protein complexes.","addition_date":"2019-05-31T12:55:57Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:StructAlign","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://mouse.genebee.msu.ru/tools/StructAlign/StructAlign_feedback.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Multiple sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492"},{"term":"Protein fold recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303"},{"term":"Structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0295"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"StructAlign","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1134/S0006297915110073","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 Pleiades Publishing, Ltd.Comparative analysis of structures of complexes of homologous proteins with DNA is important in the analysis of DNA-protein recognition. Alignment is a necessary stage of the analysis. An alignment is a matching of amino acid residues and nucleotides of one complex to residues and nucleotides of the other. Currently, there are no programs available for aligning structures of DNA-protein complexes. We present the program StructAlign, which should fill this gap. The program inputs a pair of complexes of DNA double helix with proteins and outputs an alignment of DNA chains corresponding to the best spatial fit of the protein chains.","authors":[{"name":"Alexeevski A.V."},{"name":"Galitsyna A.A."},{"name":"Karyagina A.S."},{"name":"Popov Y.V."},{"name":"Spirin S.A."}],"date":"2015-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Biochemistry (Moscow)","title":"StructAlign, a prog